            <ArticleTitle>Substituted biaryl pyrazoles as sodium channel blockers.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>5480-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bmcl.2010.07.080</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Voltage-gated sodium channels have been shown to play a critical role in neuropathic pain. A series of low molecular weight biaryl substituted pyrazole carboxamides were identified with good in-vitro potency and in-vivo efficacy. Compound 26, a Nav1.7 blocker has excellent efficacy in the Chung model of neuropathic pain.</AbstractText>
